# Build artifacts
target/
**/target/

# The per-dependency license inventory `cargo about` renders from the locked
# dependency graph into every release archive and Debian package. A build
# output, not source: `tools/release/about.toml` and `tools/release/about.hbs` are what is
# tracked, and the release workflow regenerates the file on each runner. A
# committed copy could silently disagree with the graph it claims to describe.
/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
.cursor/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Local assistant-tool state (local settings + per-agent worktrees + scheduled tasks lock)
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Rust
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock
!/Cargo.lock
# examples/go2 is an ISOLATED workspace that resolves its own lockfile - an
# unpinned fresh resolve pulls zenoh 1.9.0, which unavoidably ships
# RUSTSEC-2026-0041 (its own lz4_flex ^0.10 rollback). Track the pinned
# lockfile so builds are deny-clean by construction; after any dep change
# re-pin with `cargo update -p zenoh --precise 1.8.0` (see the lz4_flex note
# under `[advisories]` in tools/release/deny.toml).
!/examples/go2/Cargo.lock
# examples/* are likewise ISOLATED workspaces (root Cargo.toml `exclude`)
# that resolve their own lockfiles - a fresh resolve pulls zenoh 1.9.0
# (RUSTSEC-2026-0041 lz4_flex rollback). Commit pinned lockfiles (zenoh
# =1.8.0, the same pin as examples/go2) so first-touch example builds are
# advisory-clean by construction; after any dep change re-pin via
# `cargo update -p zenoh --precise 1.8.0` inside each example.
!/examples/basic_timer/Cargo.lock
!/examples/camera_pipeline/Cargo.lock
!/examples/obstacle_avoidance/Cargo.lock
!/examples/perception/Cargo.lock
!/examples/realsense/Cargo.lock
!/examples/v4l2_camera/Cargo.lock

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Quality loop progress tracking
.ralph-progress.json

# (The benches/cerulion_round_trip{,_quiescent} ignore blocks were removed
# with those trees when the latency suite replaced them; benches/latency
# carries its own results hygiene via its results/ layout.)

# Agent docs: personal assistant instructions + maintainer notes stay untracked.
# `AGENTS.md` (root + scoped) is the tracked guidance; `CLAUDE.md` files are
# one-line shims that import it. `.agents-tokens.local` is the name-class token
# list `tools/scripts/check_agents_md.sh` scrubs with - the list is itself internal
# vocabulary, so it never ships in the script or the repo.
CLAUDE.local.md
notes/
.agents-tokens.local
# The leak guard's private pattern list (`tools/scripts/leak_scan.py`), when a
# contributor keeps it inside the checkout and points LEAK_PATTERNS_FILE at it.
# The list names what the guard scrubs, so it never ships.
.leak-patterns.local
